<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rechila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 448</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rechila was king of the Suebi in Gallaecia from 438 to 448. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, he campaigned south, defeating a Roman force on the Genil, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerita-augusta">Emerita Augusta</a> in 439 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> in 441, so that Suebic power extended over much of Lusitania, Baetica and Carthaginiensis. He was the last pagan king of the Suebi; his son and successor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rechiar">Rechiar</a> was a Catholic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rechila.jpg" alt="Rechila" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Vigo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rechila.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
